shell/shaders/wallpaper-transition.frag and zesti/wallfx.py adapt the GPL-3.0
shader and subject/contagion map generator from Diego Malagrida's pocket-dots:
https://github.com/diegoMalagrida/pocket-dots (reference commit f148029).
Zestify supplies native image/video textures, owns the XDG cache/runtime,
and serializes preparation across displays.

zesti/palette.py adapts Caelestia CLI's GPL-3.0-only source-colour scoring,
smart colourfulness thresholds, hard-flavour surface adjustments, and
Gruvbox terminal-colour harmonization from utils/material/{score,generator}.py,
utils/colourfulness.py, and utils/wallpaper.py:
https://github.com/caelestia-dots/cli (reference commit 7fa3fc1).
Palette generation uses materialyoucolor directly, with no Caelestia runtime
dependency. The all-black scoring fallback is adapted to avoid recursion.

